      "text": "The wristwatch emerged from practicality (WWI), was industrialized by Swiss geography and labor organization, reached a technical apex in the mid-20th century complications arms race, survived the quartz crisis through positioning as luxury artifact rather than time-telling instrument, and now constitutes a ~$10B+ annual market in which accuracy is largely irrelevant to pricing."
    },
