      "text": "**Pre-war context:** Wristwatches were considered jewelry for women. Serious men used pocket watches — reliable, accurate, long-running, with visible seconds hands for timing. The wristwatch was seen as effeminate and impractical (the crown and setting mechanism are vulnerable when exposed on the wrist)."
