      "text": "**WWI changes everything:** Synchronized military operations require officers to know the exact time without fumbling for a pocket watch while also handling a map, compass, and sidearm. Artillery barrages are timed to the second. Machine gun teams coordinate on precise windows. The wristwatch — strapped to the left wrist, readable with a glance — is immediately more practical."
    },
