      },
      "text": "┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      TRENCH WATCH (WWI)                        │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Wire lugs: soldered or riveted loops for permanent strap       │\n│  (pocket watches adapted by adding wire cages, pre-war)        │\n│                                                                │\n│  Luminous dial: Radium paint on hands and indices              │\n│  (Ra-226, T½ = 1600 yr; intensely radioactive; later replaced  │\n│   by tritium/H-3, then strontium aluminate phosphors today)    │\n│                                                                │\n│  Shrapnel guard: Metal cage over mineral crystal               │\n│  (broken crystal in action = unusable watch)                   │\n│                                                                │\n│  Screw-back or snap-back cases: sealed against mud and water   │\n│                                                                │\n│  Large crown: gloves-on winding/setting                        │\n│                                                                │\n│  Bold Arabic numerals: legibility in poor light                │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
